e unique box-wide.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"deploy","askable":false,"exit":1,"fix":"Commit a lockfile (npm install --package-lock-only) and build again: k2 app build <folder>","http":422,"id":"lockfile_required","status":"live","what":"The folder has a package.json but no lockfile; a build in the wall installs only what is pinned.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"deploy","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Keep one manifest: drop --manifest, or make the folder's manifest.json match it, then run the command again.","http":409,"id":"manifest_conflict","status":"live","what":"The folder's own manifest.json differs from the one passed with --manifest.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"deploy","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Check it: k2 app validate <folder>. Fix what it names, then deploy again.","http":409,"id":"manifest_invalid","status":"live","what":"The App's manifest.json is missing a field, has a bad value, or asks for something this engine can't run.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"deploy","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Deploy the Seed you want: k2 app deploy <app-id> <folder|seed>. Past deploys: k2 app history <app-id>","http":409,"id":"nothing_to_roll_back","status":"live","what":"There is no earlier version to go back to (no Seed deployed yet, or the old instance is gone).","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"deploy","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner sets up what it names, then install or deploy again. K2 doesn't turn these on by itself.","http":409,"id":"requires_unmet","status":"live","what":"The Seed needs something this box doesn't have (Sew, voice or a Postgres major). The refusal names it and the fix.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"deploy","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Deploy a Seed that declares dataDown, or roll the data back first. Past deploys: k2 app history <app-id>","http":409,"id":"rollback_crosses_migration","status":"live","what":"The target Seed is at an older data revision than the live one; rolling back code doesn't roll back data.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"deploy","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Go back to a Seed that's still kept (k2 app history <app-id> marks them), or deploy the old code again from its source: k2 app deploy <app-id> <folder>","http":409,"id":"rollback_seed_gone","status":"live","what":"That version's Seed was freed: K2 keeps the Seeds of each App's last 5 deployments. The refusal names what you can still go back to.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"deploy","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Build it again from the folder (k2 app build <folder>) and deploy the new hash.","http":409,"id":"seed_corrupt","status":"live","what":"The stored Seed's files don't match its hash, so K2 won't deploy it.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"deploy","askable":false,"exit":1,"fix":"Fix each error the report names (k2 app validate <folder>), then build and deploy again.","http":422,"id":"seed_invalid","status":"live","what":"The Seed's validate report has errors, so it can't be deployed. The report comes with the refusal.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"deploy","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Build one and use the hash it prints: k2 app build <folder>","http":404,"id":"seed_not_found","status":"live","what":"No Seed with that hash (or prefix) on this box.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"deploy","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"To add a public URL, don't reinstall: k2 app expose <app-id> --tunnel. To uninstall anyway: k2 app uninstall <app-id> --drop-access","http":409,"id":"uninstall_drops_access","status":"live","what":"Uninstalling the App would drop who may use it (logins, roles, chat, shared secrets); a reinstall is a new App and gets none of it back. The refusal lists what.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"catalog","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Install it without the domain, then add yours: k2 app domain add <app-id> <host>","http":400,"id":"custom_domain_later","status":"live","what":"A catalog App can't take your 