un the command again.","http":503,"id":"app_db_vault_closed","status":"live","what":"The vault is closed, and an App's database URL lives there.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"database","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read the hint; check k2 db status and k2 vault status, then run the command again. If it repeats, report it.","http":502,"id":"app_db_failed","status":"live","what":"Postgres or the vault refused a step of connecting. The hint says which and why.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"runtime","askable":false,"exit":1,"fix":"Read why: k2 app logs <app-id> and k2 app errors <app-id>. Fix it, then deploy again.","http":409,"id":"crashlooping","status":"live","what":"The App crashed 6 times in an hour, so K2 stopped restarting it.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"runtime","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Wait a minute and run the command again. If it stays, check k2 app engine status and report it.","http":409,"id":"engine_caller_refused","status":"live","what":"The App engine refused this daemon as its caller, for example mid hand-off after a K2 update. Not the App's fault.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"runtime","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Check the box can reach K2's download host, then run k2 app engine install again (or --from <dir>).","http":409,"id":"engine_download_failed","status":"live","what":"K2 couldn't download the App engine.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"runtime","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read the error, then run k2 app engine install again. If it repeats, check k2 app engine status and report it.","http":409,"id":"engine_install_failed","status":"live","what":"The root helper couldn't install the App engine. The refusal says why.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"runtime","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"See its state: k2 app engine status. The owner reinstalls it with k2 app engine install.","http":409,"id":"engine_not_answering","status":"live","what":"The App engine is missing or doesn't answer on its socket. 