xit":3,"fix":"Ask your owner: Workspace settings → Agent → Apps, or k2 app access <workspace> --build on (the owner's own terminal, outside K2).","http":403,"id":"apps_manage_off","status":"live","what":"\"Build and run Apps\" (or \"…and manage them end to end\") is off for this agent.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"access","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Send a longer password (the refusal says the minimum).","http":400,"id":"bad_password","status":"live","what":"The test guest's password is too short.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"access","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read the reason and run the command again. See what is granted: k2 app grants <app-id>","http":409,"id":"grant_failed","status":"live","what":"K2 couldn't apply the grant. The refusal carries the reason.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"access","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Ask for it: k2 app grant <app-id> --kind guests-rooms (or --kind guests-chat, the owner's).","http":403,"id":"grant_required","status":"live","what":"The App has no grant for this (guests:rooms or guests:chat).","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"access","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Ask an Admin or the owner to make the change.","http":403,"id":"member_read_only","status":"live","what":"Members can see Apps but not change them.","who":"admin"},{"aliases":[],"area":"access","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Ask for one password set instead (k2 app user password <username> --password-stdin), or ask your human to put an email on the login (k2 app user email <username> --email <address>), then ask for the reset again.","http":409,"id":"no_email","status":"live","what":"The login has no email on file, so a one-time reset link has nowhere to go. Nothing was sent.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"access","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"List them: k2 app test-guests <app-id>","http":404,"id":"not_a_test_guest","status":"live","what":"That user isn't a test guest of this App you can change.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"access","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Ask the owner. The refusal names where they do it.","http":403,"id":"owner_only","status":"live","what":"Only the server's owner can do this (in person, from Settings or a terminal outside K2).","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"access","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Ask the owner or an admin in your Thread to run the command the refusal names, from a terminal outside K2.","http":403,"id":"person_only","status":"live","what":"A person does this, in person with a confirm: never an agent or a K2 terminal (an App's start level or keep days raised, a Space's recording raised, the CUI/FCI lock, the org's recording policies).","who":"person"},{"aliases":[],"area":"access","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner turns both on: k2 app access <workspace> --build on --manage on (the owner's own terminal, outside K2).","http":409,"id":"parent_switch_off","status":"live","what":"\"…and manage them end to end\" sits under \"Build and run Apps\", which is off.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"access","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Use one of the App's roles, or create one: k2 app role create <name> --app <app-id>","http":400,"id":"role_not_this_apps","status":"live","what":"A test guest gets one of this App's own roles (or none), and that role isn't one.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"access","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Remove one first. List them: k2 app test-guests <app-id>","http":409,"id":"too_many_test_guests","status":"live","what":"The App already has as many test guests as it may.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"access","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Check the name: k2 workspace list","http":404,"id":"workspace_not_found","status":"live","what":"No workspace by that name or id on this server.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"access","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run k2 app from the workspace's own agent terminal, or as the owner.","http":403,"id":"wrong_credential","status":"live","what":"App passes, API keys and API sessions can't manage Apps or exec into them.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"approvals","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Ask again; the owner approves the new request.","http":409,"id":"app_changed","status":"live","what":"The App is a different one now than when the request was made, so nothing was applied.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"approvals","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Ask again so the owner sees the current list: k2 app grant copy-host <app-id>","http":409,"id":"logins_changed","status":"live","what":"The box logins to copy changed since the request, so nothing was copied.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"approvals","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Update K2 (k2 update), then ask again.","http":409,"id":"no_applier","status":"live","what":"Nothing on this daemon applies this kind of request yet.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"approvals","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"See where it stands: k2 app approvals --all","http":409,"id":"not_pending","status":"live","what":"The request was already decided, revoked or expired.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"approvals","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Look up the inner code (k2 explain <code>), fix that, then ask again.","http":409,"id":"replay_failed","status":"live","what":"The request was approved, but running it now was refused. The inner code and hint come with it.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"approvals","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Ask again.","http":410,"id":"request_expired","status":"live","what":"The request waited 7 days and expired.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"approvals","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"List them: k2 app approvals --all","http":404,"id":"request_not_found","status":"live","what":"No App request with that id.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"approvals","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read the reason, fix what it names, then ask again: k2 app role room <role> <room> --caps … (or --clear).","http":409,"id":"role_room_failed","status":"live","what":"The owner approved a room line on a role of your App, but writing it was refused (the room or its caps no longer fit). The reason comes with the refusal.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"approvals","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Withdraw one (k2 app deny <id>) or wait for the owner. Yours: k2 app approvals","http":429,"id":"too_many_pending","status":"live","what":"Too many requests like this already wait for the owner.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"approvals","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read the reason (k2 explain <code> for the inner code), fix what it names, then run the same k2 app user command again; the owner approves the new request.","http":409,"id":"user_change_failed","status":"live","what":"The owner approved a change to a login of your App (add, remove, role, reset or password), but carrying it out was refused, so nothing changed. The inner code and reason come with the refusal.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"approvals","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner runs the command in person; it asks for the confirm (for example k2 app approve <id>).","http":403,"id":"vault_confirm_required","status":"live","what":"This needs a fresh owner confirm (Touch ID, the login or the vault password). A confirm works once, within 60 seconds.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"approvals","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner runs the step in person (for example k2 vault recovery show-once or k2 users set-role <login> owner); it asks for the check. Agents: don't run it, and don't change logins for it; tell your owner.","http":403,"id":"vault_presence_required","status":"live","what":"This step needs this computer's own user check (Touch ID or the Mac's password, Windows Hello, or a Linux server's owner login password): until a recovery key is confirmed, the vault's first password, recovery words, backups, box-move exports and backup keys; with the owner token, making or re-keying an owner login. A check works once, in 60 seconds. With none for the caller here: 409.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"approvals","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Ask for it: k2 app config <app-id> --isolation <level>. The owner approves it.","http":409,"id":"widening_held","status":"live","what":"The change lowers the App's wall, so it can't be applied directly; it goes through config, held for the owner.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner resumes it: k2 app resume <app-id> (or the App's own agent, if it suspended it itself).","http":409,"id":"app_suspended","status":"live","what":"The App is suspended: deploys and starts are frozen.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run it again in a moment. If it stays, report it.","http":503,"id":"audit_unavailable","status":"live","what":"K2 couldn't open the App's audit log.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Add the capability to the App's manifest and deploy again; the owner approves it once.","http":403,"id":"cap_not_granted","status":"live","what":"The App's pass doesn't carry the capability this call needs.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Sign the person in and send their session pass (Authorization: Bearer k2skn_…).","http":403,"id":"guest_required","status":"live","what":"This route is a guest's own: it needs the person's session pass, not an App or owner credential.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run it again: k2 app link <app-id> --rotate. If it repeats, report it.","http":409,"id":"link_unavailable","status":"live","what":"K2 couldn't make a new gateway link for the App.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Call it from the App's server side with its own pass.","http":403,"id":"not_exposed","status":"live","what":"app.self and app.usage answer only the App's own pass on its gateway link, never a guest.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Use the App key ($K2_SECRETS_DIR/K2_APP_KEY) on /v1/apps/$K2_APP_ID/…, or: k2 app clean-mode <app> off","http":403,"id":"owner_token_from_app","status":"live","what":"The App runs in clean mode, and Apps can't use the owner token.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read me.get again and redraw from it. Don't reopen this socket. Details: k2 study app-surfaces","http":403,"id":"access_lost","status":"live","what":"This open socket's room or capability was taken away. The pass still works.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Sign in again to get a new pass.","http":401,"id":"pass_invalid","status":"live","what":"The pass is expired or revoked, or its App is gone.","who":"person"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Send the person's session pass (Authorization: Bearer k2skn_…).","http":401,"id":"pass_required","status":"live","what":"No pass came with the request.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Send this App's own pass, or a session pass of a person signed in to this App (each App's server uses its own link).","http":403,"id":"pass_wrong_link","status":"live","what":"This pass belongs to another App or link, so this App's link refuses it.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run it with the yes: k2 app seal rotate <app-id> --yes","http":409,"id":"signout_confirm_required","status":"live","what":"Rotating the seal key signs everyone out, so it needs a yes.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Call it with the App's pass or the guest's session pass.","http":403,"id":"skin_token","status":"live","what":"This route answers only a live App pass or a guest pass (k2skn_).","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"door","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner resumes it: k2 app resume <app-id>","http":409,"id":"suspended","status":"live","what":"The App is suspended, so this is frozen until it is resumed.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"data","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Start it: k2 app start <app-id>","http":409,"id":"app_not_running","status":"live","what":"The App isn't running, so there is nothing to exec into.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"data","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"List what is there: k2 app data ls <app-id> [<path>]","http":404,"id":"data_not_found","status":"live","what":"That path isn't in the App's data folder.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"data","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read the reason, fix it (path, space, the App running), then run k2 app data put again.","http":409,"id":"data_put_failed","status":"live","what":"Copying into the App's data folder failed. The refusal says why.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"data","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Split or compress it inside the App first (k2 app exec <app-id> -- …), then get the parts.","http":413,"id":"data_too_large","status":"live","what":"The file is bigger than k2 app data get reads back.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"data","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Deploy it guarded: k2 app deploy <app-id> <folder|seed> --engine guarded. Logs work anyway: k2 app logs <app-id>","http":409,"id":"exec_unavailable","status":"live","what":"Exec and shell reach only a guarded container, and this App isn't one (process engine, process exception, or not redeployed).","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"data","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Use the CLI, which opens the WebSocket: k2 app shell <app-id>","http":400,"id":"websocket_required","status":"live","what":"k2 app shell is a WebSocket on the daemon's TCP port; a plain request can't open it.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"egress","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Ask only for public hosts: k2 app egress add <app-id> <host[:port]>","http":400,"id":"egress_host_invalid","status":"live","what":"That host is a private, local or metadata address; Apps never reach those.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"egress","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Drop it; call K2 on the App's gateway link instead.","http":400,"id":"egress_self","status":"live","what":"That host is this box. An App reaches K2 through its gateway, never the egress proxy.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"egress","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Ask for the hosts it needs: k2 app egress add <app-id> <host[:port]>","http":409,"id":"open_path_only","status":"live","what":"Broad egress belongs to the open path, and this App is guarded.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Stop every App first (k2 app stop <app-id>), then run k2 app box unprep --yes.","http":409,"id":"apps_running","status":"live","what":"Apps still run, so the box setup can't be undone. The refusal lists them.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Fix what that step needs, then run k2 app box prepare again (--dry-run shows every change).","http":409,"id":"box_prep_failed","status":"live","what":"Box prep stopped at one step. The refusal names it.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Fix what the refusal names: k2 app box-service request <app-id> <name> [<host-port>] [--app-port N]","http":400,"id":"box_service_invalid","status":"live","what":"The box service request is malformed: a bad name, protocol or port.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Pick another service or port. See this App's: k2 app box-service <app-id>","http":403,"id":"box_service_refused","status":"live","what":"That port can never be a box service. The refusal says why.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run k2 app box unprep --yes (--dry-run lists what it undoes).","http":409,"id":"confirm_needed","status":"live","what":"Undoing the box setup needs a confirm.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"See usage: k2 app resources. Free space, or pass --disk-override \"<reason>\" (held for the owner unless you are the owner).","http":409,"id":"disk_low","status":"live","what":"The box's disk is past the line for new disk work. The refusal names the biggest users.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner runs k2 root-helper update, or the one root step the refusal prints (in an SSH session).","http":409,"id":"helper_needed","status":"live","what":"This step needs a newer K2 root helper than the box has.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run it on a Linux K2 box.","http":409,"id":"linux_only","status":"live","what":"This runs on Linux boxes only.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Free space on the box (k2 app resources shows usage), then run k2 app box prepare again.","http":409,"id":"low_disk","status":"live","what":"The disk is nearly full, so box prep won't start.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Check the box can reach K2's download host, then run k2 app box prepare --install-podman again.","http":409,"id":"podman_download_failed","status":"live","what":"K2 couldn't download or check its Podman bundle.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner runs k2 app box prepare --install-podman (--dry-run shows every change first).","http":409,"id":"podman_install_needed","status":"live","what":"The box's Podman is too old for Apps (they need Podman 5+).","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read the reason, then run k2 app box podman uninstall again (the owner, outside K2).","http":409,"id":"podman_uninstall_failed","status":"live","what":"Removing K2's Podman failed. The refusal says why.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Pick another port, or ask that App's agent (k2 msg <address> \"…\") or the owner.","http":409,"id":"port_owned","status":"live","what":"Another App on this box already opens that port. The refusal names it and its agent.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Ask someone with that role to do it: an Admin or the owner.","http":403,"id":"role_required","status":"live","what":"Your login's role on this server is too low for this. The refusal names the role it needs.","who":"admin"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Wait for it to finish, then run the command again.","http":409,"id":"root_busy","status":"live","what":"Another root step (box prep, an engine install, mail setup) is running.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read the reason, fix it, then run k2 app box unprep --yes again.","http":409,"id":"unprep_failed","status":"live","what":"Undoing the box setup failed. The refusal says why.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"box","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run Apps on an x86_64 or aarch64 Linux box.","http":409,"id":"unsupported","status":"live","what":"K2 has no build of this piece for this box's CPU (x86_64 and aarch64 only).","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Deploy it and wait until it's live (k2 app deployment <app-id> <id>; k2 app logs <app-id>), then run this again.","http":409,"id":"app_not_healthy","status":"live","what":"The App isn't live, so it can't take or serve a label yet.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"See the App's names: k2 app domains <app-id>. A new zone: the owner runs k2 domain add <apex> first.","http":409,"id":"domain_not_attached","status":"live","what":"No attached domain covers that host, or the App has no such custom domain.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Ask again.","http":409,"id":"holder_changed","status":"live","what":"The label's holder changed since the request, so nothing moved.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Check the spelling: k2 app domain add <app-id> <subdomain|host>","http":400,"id":"invalid_domain","status":"live","what":"That isn't a valid hostname.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Pick a new label, or ask the owner to move it deliberately (--transfer, from the owner's own terminal, outside K2).","http":403,"id":"label_exists_elsewhere","status":"live","what":"The label already serves something on this box that isn't your workspace's; an agent never repoints it.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read the reason and run the command again. See the App's names: k2 app domains <app-id>","http":409,"id":"label_move_failed","status":"live","what":"K2 couldn't move the label; it still serves what it served before. The refusal says why.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"See what it serves: k2 app domains <app-id>","http":404,"id":"label_not_taken","status":"live","what":"The App doesn't serve that label, so there is nothing to return.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Pick another label, or ask that workspace's agent. Moving one across workspaces is the owner's hand-over.","http":403,"id":"label_owned_by_other_workspace","status":"live","what":"The label belongs to another workspace; an App only takes its own workspace's labels.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Remove it there first: k2 app domain rm <other-app> <label>","http":409,"id":"label_serves_another_app","status":"live","what":"The label already serves another App.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Start it (k2 publish start <label>), then run k2 app label return <app-id> <label>.","http":409,"id":"legacy_not_running","status":"live","what":"The old --cmd service isn't answering (or was removed), so the label can't move back to it.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Point what calls it at the App's front port instead.","http":409,"id":"no_public_label","status":"live","what":"The service runs without a public hostname (--no-tunnel), so there is no label to move.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Pick another subdomain: k2 app domain add <app-id> <subdomain>","http":400,"id":"reserved_label","status":"live","what":"That label is reserved and can't be used.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Remove one first: k2 app domain rm <app-id> <host>. See them: k2 app domains <app-id>","http":409,"id":"too_many_custom_domains","status":"live","what":"This box serves as many custom App names as it may.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"domains","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Your --cmd service's label: k2 app label take <app-id> <label>. Another service: stop it there first.","http":409,"id":"use_label_take","status":"live","what":"That label is a published service's in your workspace; domain add doesn't take it.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"handover","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner gives it to a workspace: k2 app unpark <app-id> --to <workspace>","http":409,"id":"app_parked","status":"live","what":"The App is parked: stopped and held by the server's owner.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"handover","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read the reason, then run the move step again: k2 app move-plan <service> --app <app-id>","http":409,"id":"copy_host_failed","status":"live","what":"Copying the box logins' grants to the App failed. The refusal says why.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"handover","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Clear what it lists, or move the App by hand: the refusal's manual steps (a new App id, its data, labels and domains).","http":409,"id":"handoff_needs_v1","status":"live","what":"The App has something a hand-over wouldn't carry yet (guests tied to the old workspace, its own labels or domains…). The refusal lists each blocker.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"handover","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Give them a role of this App (k2 app role create <name> --app <app-id>, then k2 app grant role <grant-id> --role <name>), or take the room off those roles (k2 app role room <role> <handle> --clear), then ask again.","http":409,"id":"handover_shared_roles","status":"live","what":"The App's guests hold box-wide roles that name the old agent's room. After a hand-over they'd keep talking to the old agent.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"handover","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Wait until K2 has finished starting (k2 vault status), then run it again.","http":503,"id":"handover_vault_closed","status":"live","what":"The vault isn't open, so the hand-over can't move the App's keys.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"handover","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Fix what the step names, then run the plan again: k2 app move-plan <service> --app <app-id>","http":409,"id":"move_step_failed","status":"live","what":"A step of the move failed; the rest didn't run. The refusal names the step and why.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"handover","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Check the name: move-plan takes a --cmd service or a --skin site. Moving one in: k2 study app-move","http":409,"id":"not_a_cmd_service","status":"live","what":"That service is an App's own service, so there is nothing to move.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"handover","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run the take again so the owner sees the current list: k2 app label take <app-id> <label>","http":409,"id":"site_guests_changed","status":"live","what":"The --skin site's guests changed since the owner approved the move, so nothing was copied and the label didn't move.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"handover","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run the take again; if it fails again, the refusal says why (k2 app label take <app-id> <label>).","http":500,"id":"site_copy_failed","status":"live","what":"K2 couldn't copy the --skin site's guests onto the App, so the label didn't move.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"handover","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Request again so the owner sees the current list: k2 app move-plan <service> --app <app-id> --request","http":409,"id":"plan_changed","status":"live","what":"The box-login users to copy changed since the request, so nothing was copied.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"push","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read counts instead: k2 app push status <app>","http":403,"id":"admin_only","status":"live","what":"Push devices are the owner's and Admins' to see.","who":"admin"},{"aliases":[],"area":"push","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Send it from the App's server side with its own pass.","http":403,"id":"app_pass_required","status":"live","what":"Only the App's own pass, on its link, sends notifications; a guest never does.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"push","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Register your own app instead (channel app).","http":400,"id":"channel_unavailable","status":"live","what":"K2 Companion can't receive this App's notifications yet.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"push","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Raise the limit (k2 app push set <app> --max-devices N), or remove a device: k2 app push devices rm <app> <apd_…>","http":409,"id":"push_devices_full","status":"live","what":"The App holds as many push devices as its owner allows.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"push","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Add it: k2 app push setup <app> (--apns-key … or --fcm-service-account …). Check: k2 app push status <app>","http":409,"id":"push_not_configured","status":"live","what":"The App has no push key for that platform.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"push","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Send the device token to your App's server; it calls K2 as that person (k2.asGuest(pass).push.register). To change it: k2 app push set <app> --register any","http":403,"id":"push_server_only","status":"live","what":"This App takes push.register and push.viewing only from its own server, never a phone calling K2 directly.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"push","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Sign them out first (the App calls push.unregister on sign-out), then register again.","http":409,"id":"token_in_use","status":"live","what":"Another person on this App is still signed in with this phone's push token.","who":"person"},{"aliases":[],"area":"pairing","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Type the password again.","http":401,"id":"bad_login","status":"live","what":"The password is wrong.","who":"person"},{"aliases":[],"area":"pairing","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The App's owner turns it on: k2 app stay-signed-in <app> <days>","http":409,"id":"device_signin_off","status":"live","what":"The App's \"Stay signed in\" is off, so a phone can't stay signed in.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"pairing","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Use one of the App's pairing hosts: k2 app pairing status <app>","http":400,"id":"host_not_paired","status":"live","what":"That host isn't one this App pairs on.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"pairing","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Wait and try again later, or ask the App's owner to unlock the user: k2 app user unlock <username>","http":423,"id":"locked","status":"live","what":"Too many wrong passwords, so sign-in is locked for a while.","who":"person"},{"aliases":[],"area":"pairing","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Give it a label (k2 app domain add <app> <subdomain>, needs K2 Connect), then run k2 app pairing setup <app>.","http":409,"id":"no_public_host","status":"live","what":"The App has no public k2.dev host to pair on.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"pairing","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Name an App, not host.","http":400,"id":"not_for_host","status":"live","what":"Pairing and push are for a published App's own users, never the box login.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"pairing","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Start again from the web App to get a fresh code.","http":401,"id":"pair_code_invalid","status":"live","what":"The code is unknown, used, expired or for another App.","who":"person"},{"aliases":[],"area":"pairing","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Start from the person's web sign-in.","http":403,"id":"pairing_from_device","status":"live","what":"A phone that is signed in can't pair another phone.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"pairing","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Redeem it from the phone app. Webview origins: k2 app pairing setup <app> --native-origin <origin>","http":403,"id":"pairing_not_from_browser","status":"live","what":"A phone app redeems the code, never a web page.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"pairing","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"See why: k2 app pairing check <app>. Pairing needs a runtime App with K2's front (host.clientIp on).","http":409,"id":"pairing_not_served","status":"live","what":"K2 doesn't serve this App's phone link files now, so phones can't pair.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"pairing","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The App's owner turns it on: k2 app pairing setup <app>. Server-wide off (K2_APP_PAIRING=off) is the owner's.","http":403,"id":"pairing_off","status":"live","what":"Phone pairing is off for this App (or for the whole server).","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"pairing","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Ask the person for the password and send it with the call (pairing.start, profile.deleteAccount).","http":401,"id":"reauth_required","status":"live","what":"The sign-in is more than 15 minutes old.","who":"person"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Ask for that many days or fewer (k2 app recording <app> shows orgAudioMaxDays), or the owner raises the server's: k2 hostchat recording policy set recording.audio_max_days N","http":400,"id":"above_org_audio_max_days","status":"live","what":"An App's recording audio keep days can't be above the server's own recording.audio_max_days.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Leave the agent out of chat.setChannels. To put an agent in a channel, list it in the manifest's chat block (agents: [...]).","http":403,"id":"agent_subject","status":"live","what":"That username is an agent's login. Agents chat as themselves (k2 chat); an App never signs one in or sets its channels.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Name one of this App's Spaces (k2 app chat <app> lists them), or leave space out when the App has only one.","http":409,"id":"app_mismatch","status":"live","what":"That Space belongs to another App. An App acts only in its own Spaces.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Use another slug for the new channel, or keep the type the channel has.","http":409,"id":"channel_type_mismatch","status":"live","what":"A channel with that slug already exists with the other type (text or voice); Sew never changes a channel's type.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":true,"exit":3,"fix":"You ask, the owner allows: run the Ask with: line the error ends with (k2 permission request chat.account scope=coworker). Or the owner runs k2 app grant add --kind chat --subject-kind workspace --subject <ws> --scope coworker. Then run it again.","http":403,"id":"chat_account_needed","status":"live","what":"The agent has no chat account of its own, and the call needs one: Sew makes the agent that creates a Space (k2 chat space create, --app too) its manager. \"Manage Chat / Voice Hosting\" makes the account by itself, so a person removed or turned off this one.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":1,"fix":"Run the command again in a few seconds. If it stays like this past a minute, tell your human (k2 hostchat status shows Sew's health).","http":409,"id":"chat_account_pending","status":"live","what":"The agent's chat account is granted, and Sew is still setting it up.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner gives it one, in person: k2 app grant <app> --kind chat-key (an agent asks on a card: k2 permission request apps.chat-key app=<app>).","http":409,"id":"chat_key_required","status":"live","what":"The App has no chat key, so it can't set its people's channels or make channels in its Spaces.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner sets it up (k2 hostchat status shows what is missing); if it is set up, try again in a moment.","http":409,"id":"chat_unavailable","status":"live","what":"Chat / Voice Hosting isn't set up on this server (or K2 can't read its chat store right now).","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Use another App for the chat key, or the owner moves the home client first: k2 hostchat home client <app>|none","http":409,"id":"home_client_cannot_govern","status":"live","what":"The App is the chat install's home client (it sees every Space a person is in), so it can't hold a chat key or govern a Space.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":1,"fix":"principal_unknown on managers.0: your agent needs its own chat account (k2 permission request chat.account scope=coworker). On owner_external_id: the --owner person has no chat yet; the owner gives it (k2 app user chat <user> member --app <app>). Else fix that value.","http":422,"id":"invalid_state","status":"live","what":"Sew (or K2) can't do it in the current state. error.details has reason and field (the value it is about). principal_unknown: Sew has no chat account for that person or agent. member_not_provisioned: the account isn't set up yet (retry in a few seconds). target_not_eligible: that member can't take the role (an assistant is never a manager).","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner approves the App's chat caps (k2 app approvals; k2 app approve <id>), or name them: k2 app grant <app> --kind chat-key --caps \"chat:read chat:post\"","http":409,"id":"no_chat_caps","status":"live","what":"The App's manifest chat caps aren't approved yet (or the App is suspended), so a chat key has nothing to grant.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner or an Admin switches it, in person: k2 hostchat app-space governance <app> <space> app (an agent asks on a card: k2 permission request sew.space-governance).","http":409,"id":"not_app_governed","status":"live","what":"The Space is still governed by Sew's own roles, so the App can't make channels or set who is in them yet.","who":"admin"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run Sew under K2 to use chat keys (k2 study app-chat). Until then the App's chat goes through Sew's own logins.","http":409,"id":"provider_is_standalone","status":"live","what":"This box's Sew is a standalone install: it takes no K2 passes, so an App on it has no chat key.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner upgrades Sew: k2 hostchat upgrade. Then try again.","http":409,"id":"sew_feature_missing","status":"live","what":"This server's Sew is too old for what the App asked (a chat key and App-governed Spaces need Sew 0.6.0; making channels needs 0.5.0). The refusal names the feature.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read the hint: fix the op it names and send again. If it repeats, k2 hostchat status shows Sew's version and health.","http":502,"id":"sew_refused","status":"live","what":"Sew refused the call, or answered something K2 couldn't read. The hint carries Sew's own answer.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Try again in a minute. If it keeps failing, the owner checks it: k2 hostchat status (k2 hostchat restart if it is down).","http":503,"id":"sew_unreachable","status":"live","what":"K2 couldn't reach Sew (Chat / Voice Hosting) on this server.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"chat","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Make the App its own Space: k2 chat space create <slug> --name <Name> --app <app> (or bind one: k2 hostchat app-space bind <app> <space>).","http":409,"id":"space_unbound","status":"live","what":"That Space is bound to no App, or this App has no Space bound to it.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"links","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Keep the path, or drop it on purpose: pass --drop <path>.","http":409,"id":"link_path_dropped","status":"live","what":"k2 app links set would drop a link path that already shipped in a phone app.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":["pairing_needs_k2_front"],"area":"links","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Turn K2's front back on: remove host.clientIp: false from the manifest and deploy again.","http":409,"id":"needs_k2_front","status":"live","what":"Apps with host.clientIp: false get no K2 answers on their host (link files, update feed).","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"updates","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Make the archive smaller (512 MiB at most) and upload it again.","http":413,"id":"artifact_too_large","status":"live","what":"The update archive is over 512 MiB.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"updates","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Use one of: .app.tar.gz .AppImage .AppImage.tar.gz .deb .rpm .msi .exe .nsis.zip .msi.zip","http":400,"id":"artifact_type_refused","status":"live","what":"That file type isn't an update archive K2 serves.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"updates","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Add that platform's archive, or drop it on purpose: pass --drop-platform <key>.","http":409,"id":"platform_dropped","status":"live","what":"The channel's current release has a platform the new one lacks, so those users would get no update.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"updates","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Send the public key: k2 app updates key --set <public key>. Keep the secret key on the signing Mac or in the vault.","http":400,"id":"secret_key_refused","status":"live","what":"That is a minisign SECRET key. K2 takes only the App's updater public key.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"updates","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Sign that archive again with the key that matches the App's updater public key, then upload again.","http":400,"id":"signature_invalid","status":"live","what":"An archive's .sig doesn't verify against the App's updater public key. The refusal names the platform.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"updates","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run it on this server's own node (k2 compute nodes lists them).","http":403,"id":"signing_node_not_owner","status":"live","what":"A signing job may run only on this server's own node, not a shared one.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"updates","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Check the box's disk (k2 app resources), then push again.","http":500,"id":"staging_failed","status":"live","what":"K2 couldn't stage the update archives on this box's disk (the refusal says why).","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"updates","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Wait and try again later; nothing to change on the App.","http":503,"id":"updates_host_unavailable","status":"live","what":"K2's download host isn't reachable or isn't live yet, so the update feed is off.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"updates","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Push again in a moment; if it keeps failing, restart K2.","http":500,"id":"upload_spawn_failed","status":"live","what":"K2 couldn't start the upload to the download host.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"updates","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Give the release a higher semver version than the channel's current one, then publish again.","http":409,"id":"version_not_newer","status":"live","what":"The release version isn't semver, or isn't higher than the channel's current one.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"static","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Update that server's K2 (from 0.46.7 a static App deploys), or serve it with k2 publish run --skin there.","http":409,"id":"static_not_on_runtime","status":"retired","what":"An older K2 server: its App runtime didn't serve static Apps (host.mode: \"static\").","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"docs","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Change a .dxf with its edit verbs (k2 doc entity move|set|add|delete|rotate|scale, attrib set, block insert, text set; k2 doc cad --help); change a .dwg in your CAD app, and its save is taken in.","http":409,"id":"cad_writer_disabled","status":"live","what":"Nobody saves a drawing whole in K2: a .dxf changes through the edit verbs, and a .dwg is read only. A whole-file write, restore or undo of one, or an edit of a .dwg, is refused while the CAD core is on. Nothing was changed.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"docs","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read the drawing again and change it with the edit verbs instead (k2 doc cad --help).","http":409,"id":"cad_undo_not_latest","status":"live","what":"Undo goes back only from the drawing's latest change: someone changed it after the change you asked to undo, so nothing was undone.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"docs","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Read the drawing again (its new version and digest), then undo or edit from there.","http":409,"id":"cad_expect_stale","status":"live","what":"The drawing isn't the version you saw: its digest differs from the one you sent, so nothing was undone.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"homes","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Keep the group; rename or move it instead. The item comes back in rejected[] with the hint \"The People group can't be deleted.\", and the next pull brings the group back.","http":409,"id":"builtin_group","status":"live","what":"The People group is built in: every person has one, and it can't be deleted or merged away. Renaming and moving it work.","who":"person"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Nothing to change while air-gap is on. The owner turns air-gap off if this server should reach out.","http":409,"id":"airgap","status":"live","what":"Air-gap is on, so K2 makes no outside call (DNS checks, push, downloads).","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Fix what the hint names and run the command again (k2 app --help shows the shape).","http":400,"id":"bad_request","status":"live","what":"The request is missing a field or has a bad value. The hint names it.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run it again in a moment. If it repeats, report it with the hint.","http":500,"id":"db_error","status":"live","what":"K2's database refused the step.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"The owner turns it on: k2 app email on <app> --sender <address>","http":403,"id":"email_off","status":"live","what":"This App doesn't send email: its owner hasn't turned it on with a sender, or email is off on this server.","who":"owner"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run it again. If it repeats, report it with the hint.","http":500,"id":"failed","status":"live","what":"K2 hit an error building the answer.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run it from the App's own workspace with a valid passport, or ask the owner.","http":403,"id":"forbidden","status":"live","what":"This credential may not do that (an unregistered workspace, a bad token, or not the App's agent).","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run it again. If it repeats, report it with the hint.","http":500,"id":"internal","status":"live","what":"K2 hit an internal error.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Check the box's disk (k2 app resources), then run it again. If it repeats, report it.","http":500,"id":"io_error","status":"live","what":"K2 couldn't read or write a file on the box.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Use the method the hint names (a GET or a POST).","http":405,"id":"method_not_allowed","status":"live","what":"The route doesn't take that HTTP method.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Check the name or id: k2 app list","http":404,"id":"not_found","status":"live","what":"No such App, route or record.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Slow down and try again later; the hint says how often is fine.","http":429,"id":"rate_limited","status":"live","what":"Too many calls of this kind in the last hour.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run it again. If it repeats, report it with the hint.","http":500,"id":"skin_error","status":"live","what":"K2 couldn't read the App's users or grants.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Pick another username. Reserved: owner, root, admin, administrator, system, k2, and anyone who signs in to K2 itself.","http":409,"id":"login_name_reserved","status":"live","what":"A login an agent or an App key makes can't take a name people on this box sign in or stamp under.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Add it for the whole App: k2 app grant <app-id> --kind guests-rooms --room <room>. That replaces the list, so repeat the rooms it has (k2 app guest ceiling <app-id>). An agent with \"Let this agent manage its Apps' users\" on can set any room itself: k2 app user rooms.","http":403,"id":"outside_app_rooms","status":"live","what":"That room isn't one this App's own code may hand its people: not the App's own room, and not on its guests-rooms grant.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Use a room the pass holds, or have the owner add it. Agent-tied: it clears when the person chooses their own password: first sign-in with a temporary password, an invite or reset link, or the App's forgot-password flow.","http":403,"id":"skin_room","status":"live","what":"The pass doesn't hold that room or Thread (the same answer as a room that doesn't exist). A hint saying \"waiting for reset (agent-tied)\" means an agent set this login up, so that room stays held back.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Check the box's disk, then run it again. If it repeats, report it.","http":500,"id":"state_write_failed","status":"live","what":"K2 couldn't save its state for this step.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run it again in a moment. If it repeats, report it.","http":500,"id":"store","status":"live","what":"K2's store refused the step.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Send a smaller body (the hint says the limit).","http":413,"id":"too_large","status":"live","what":"The request body is over this route's limit.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":2,"fix":"Fix what the hint names; the command's --help shows the shape.","http":400,"id":"usage","status":"live","what":"The request has the wrong shape. The hint names what is expected.","who":"agent"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Wait until K2 has finished starting, then run it again (k2 vault status).","http":503,"id":"vault_closed","status":"live","what":"The vault isn't open yet.","who":"k2"},{"aliases":[],"area":"general","askable":false,"exit":3,"fix":"Run it again. If it repeats, check k2 vault status and report it.","http":500,"id":"vault_error","status":"live","what":"The vault refused the step; nothing was delivered.","who":"k2"}],"schema":1}
EOF
}
_study_page_app_errors() {
    cat <<'EOF'
k2 study app-errors — every App refusal: what happened, the fix, who fixes it

Every App route refuses with a stable id (error.code). The id never
changes, so a script or an agent can match on it. Look one up:
  k2 explain <id>          what happened, the fix, who fixes it
  k2 explain <id> --json   the same as JSON
  k2 explain               every id, by area
An App command that is refused prints fix: <the fix> before K2's own
Ask with: line, and its --json error object carries next (the fix) and
explain ("k2 explain <id>"). The exit code each id gives is beside it:
3 refused; 2 a bad request (fix the call); 1 a build or deploy that
failed (read its report or the deployment's error). k2 explain itself
exits 4 for an id it doesn't know.
When the fix is the owner's or an Admin's: if the refusal ended with an
Ask with: line, run it as printed (a permission card); otherwise tell
your human what the fix says. "retired" ids are ones older K2 servers
send; they still explain.

DEPLOY (validate, build, deploy, rollback)
  app_exists (exit 3)
      fix: Deploy to it (k2 app deploy <app-id> <folder|seed>) or pick
      another id. See what exists: k2 app list
  app_id_invalid (exit 2)
      fix: Pick a shorter, plain id (lowercase letters, digits and single
      '-') and run the command again.
  app_id_reserved (exit 2)
      fix: Pick another id. A label with that name can still move to the
      App: k2 app label take <app-id> <label>
  app_not_found (exit 3)
      fix: List the Apps you can see: k2 app list
  build_failed (exit 1)
      fix: Read the build output, fix the build in the folder, then run k2
      app build <folder> again.
  deploy_in_progress (exit 3)
      fix: Wait for it to end (k2 app history <app-id>), then run the
      command again.
  folder_outside_workspace (exit 3)
      fix: Copy or move the App's folder into your workspace, then build or
      deploy from there.
  is_an_app (exit 2)
      fix: Use the App verbs: k2 app start|stop|deploy|uninstall <app-id>
  label_taken (exit 3)
      fix: Pick another App id, or ask the label's holder. Moving your own
      label over: k2 study app-move
  lockfile_required (exit 1)
      fix: Commit a lockfile (npm install --package-lock-only) and build
      again: k2 app build <folder>
  manifest_conflict (exit 3)
      fix: Keep one manifest: drop --manifest, or make the folder's
      manifest.json match it, then run the command again.
  manifest_invalid (exit 3)
      fix: Check it: k2 app validate <folder>. Fix what it names, then
      deploy again.
  nothing_to_roll_back (exit 3)
      fix: Deploy the Seed you want: k2 app deploy <app-id> <folder|seed>.
      Past deploys: k2 app history <app-id>
  requires_unmet (exit 3)
      fix: The owner sets up what it names, then install or deploy again. K2
      doesn't turn these on by itself.
  rollback_crosses_migration (exit 3)
      fix: Deploy a Seed that declares dataDown, or roll the data back
      first. Past deploys: k2 app history <app-id>
  rollback_seed_gone (exit 3)
      fix: Go back to a Seed that's still kept (k2 app history <app-id>
      marks them), or deploy the old code again from its source: k2 app
      deploy <app-id> <folder>
  seed_corrupt (exit 3)
      fix: Build it again from the folder (k2 app build <folder>) and deploy
      the new hash.
  seed_invalid (exit 1)
      fix: Fix each error the report names (k2 app validate <folder>), then
      build and deploy again.
  seed_not_found (exit 3)
      fix: Build one and use the hash it prints: k2 app build <folder>
  uninstall_drops_access (exit 3)
      fix: To add a public URL, don't reinstall: k2 app expose <app-id>
      --tunnel. To uninstall anyway: k2 app uninstall <app-id> --drop-access

CATALOG (suite Apps from K2's catalog: k2 app catalog, install --catalog)
  custom_domain_later (exit 2)
      fix: Install it without the domain, then add yours: k2 app domain add
      <app-id> <host>
  job_corrupt (exit 3)
      fix: Start the install again: k2 app install --catalog <entry>. If it
      happens again, report it.
  job_not_found (exit 3)
      fix: List the install jobs you can see: k2 app catalog job
  not_retryable (exit 3)
      fix: See the job and its fix: k2 app catalog job <job-id>. If it
      failed for good, start a new install: k2 app install --catalog <entry>

RUNTIME (the App engine, the box, health)
  app_db_door_missing (exit 3)
      fix: The owner updates the engine (k2 app engine install), then
      re-hosts the App. For a database, connect it instead: k2 app db
      connect <app-id> --new | --db <name>.
  crashlooping (exit 1)
      fix: Read why: k2 app logs <app-id> and k2 app errors <app-id>. Fix
      it, then deploy again.
  engine_caller_refused (exit 3)
      fix: Wait a minute and run the command again. If it stays, check k2
      app engine status and report it.
  engine_download_failed (exit 3)
      fix: Check the box can reach K2's download host, then run k2 app
      engine install again (or --from <dir>).
  engine_install_failed (exit 3)
      fix: Read the error, then run k2 app engine install again. If it
      repeats, check k2 app engine status and report it.
  engine_not_answering (exit 3)
      fix: See its state: k2 app engine status. The owner reinstalls it with
      k2 app engine install.
  engine_protocol_mismatch (exit 3)
      fix: Install the matching engine: k2 app engine install (the owner).
      k2 app engine status shows both sides.
  engine_refused (exit 3)
      fix: Update K2 so the daemon and engine match (k2 update), then run k2
      app engine install again.
  engine_unavailable (exit 3)
      fix: See what is missing: k2 app engine status. Or deploy walled: k2
      app deploy <app-id> <folder|seed> --engine guarded
  health_failed (exit 1)
      fix: Read why: k2 app logs <app-id> and k2 app deployment <app-id>
